  "ground_truth": {
    "defect": true,
    "category": "auth-bypass",
    "severity": [
      "high",
      "critical"
    ],
    "explanation": "loadRecord's requireOwner option is deliberately optional: its doc comment says omitting it is reserved for internal cross-user jobs, and HTTP handlers must always pass the authenticated user's id. The existing GET /records/:id route does exactly that, and the retention job (shown here with only a metrics line added) legitimately omits it. The new export route calls loadRecord(req.params.id) with no options -- the internal-job calling convention -- so any authenticated user can export any other patient's medical record by id. Nothing in the export handler looks like a removed check; the authorization simply never attaches, and the route otherwise looks carefully built (rate limit, content-disposition, CSV headers). The tests export only the caller's own record and never attempt another user's, so the suite stays green. Recognizing the bug requires combining the loader's documented default with which call sites are HTTP-facing."
  },
